From 2e9e2465293d33391a3047b6c5285fb7c743feca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/65] Open the game display; add an SDL2 host backend

Ports H029+$1206 (screen, window, palette, mouse pointers), H029+$0408
(Allocate_GraphicRecord), H029+$1346 (offscreen View), H029+$12BC, and
the H016/H018/H021/H022/H037/H051/H055/H084 library adapters they use,
plus H024 Open_GameScreen and H025 Open_GameWindow.

On the host, src_c/readable/host emulates the NDK subset the game uses
with the same structure and function names, so the adapters are the same
on both targets, and shows the screen with SDL2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
